# .env is deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# Some platforms auto-detect a Node project and generate their own image whose
# only source of configuration is `COPY . .`. Excluding .env there leaves the
# container with no settings at all, so it starts, binds its port, and then
# reports "Crawler is disabled" on every tick without ever crawling.
#
# The trade-off: credentials are baked into the image layers. Prefer setting
# environment variables in the platform's own panel where that is an option —
# those override anything in .env.
